 of such situations will not include physical violence rather than the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T00:07:55-07:00","id":1115414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1115153#post1115153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...there's a balance here. Yes, Beasts are willing to let a lot of things slide because, hey, family-but then again, family members <i>do</i> fight over things. Family means that certain responses are off the table, but even fistfights happen between brothers and sisters(boy howdy, do they happen), and Beasts are definitely not a conventional family as we understand it now-you almost have to expect a certain amount of &quot;I'm going to make you bleed because you took my chew toy&quot; from time to time.<br /> <br /> So while a lot of it depends on how important it is to each Beast involved and why, sure, you might not have murder, but you will still realistically could have fighting happen, from social and mental to subversion to, yes, trying to beat each other into submission.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would never underestimate the violence that can happen between family. Murder is definitely on the table as a potential outcome. Cain and Abel, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T00:58:12-07:00","id":1115424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1115414#post1115414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would never underestimate the violence that can happen between family. Murder is definitely on the table as a potential outcome. Cain and Abel, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, though, this would depend far more on the <i>people</i> - that is, the Beasts - than on the lessons in question. Two Beasts who get along reasonably well by philosophically disagree on which lesson should be taught (between curiosity and caution, for instance) and two Beasts who hate each other's guts are very different situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:19:50-07:00","id":1115913,"title":"","content":"Do not underestimate the power that <span style=\"color:brown\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:mediumblue\">&lt;</span>a<span style=\"color:red\"> href<span style=\"color:mediumblue\">=&quot;</span></span></span></span></span>http://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/europe/russian-man-shot-in-quarrel-over-immanuel-kant-s-philosophy-8820327.html<span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:red\"><span style=\"color:mediumblue\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:mediumblue\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">philosphy holds</span></span></span><span style=\"color:brown\"><span style=\"font-family:Consolas\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:mediumblue\">&lt;</span>/a<span style=\"color:mediumblue\">&gt;</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T16:40:51-07:00","id":1116153,"title":"","content":"I feel that it ultimately comes down to the people behind the lessons really. Yeah, culturally Beasts try for an overall &quot;live and let live&quot; philosophy when it comes to other Beasts and monsters, but people have gone to war over sillier thing that a person's beliefs. And when it comes to the lessons a Beast teaches, often those lessons are very near and dear to the individual in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:04:42-07:00","id":1117196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1115228#post1115228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine if two Beasts ended up going after the same target there would be some conflict as soon as it was known the other was involved. Though I imagine unless it was the aforementioned case of being exceptionally opposed to the other Beast's lesson or something then it would probably just result in two arguing over who's getting the big meal and who will be stuck with leaving empty handed or just feeding through family dinner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, have I missed something? Why would one of them have to leave empty-handed? The prey 'learning a lesson' is not necessary for sating the hunger. That is mostly justification/a security measure not to attract Heroes. So... why should not both be able to feed off of the target?<br /> <br /> Not to mention that, should they really have <i>opposite lessons </i>to teach, how come they are ending up with the <i>same </i>guy? Can't rightly say I see a Beast looking to teach the lesson of Pro-Slavery to a KKK member. What kind of person would be an approrpiate candidate for the lesson of finally stopping/starting relying on others?<br /> <br /> I mean, theoretically, there is nothing stopping them, and how it turns out completely depends on the beasts in question and their relationship imo. But still, I wonder what qualities you possess to attract two Beasts at the same time for opposite reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:45:18-07:00","id":1117329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1117196#post1117196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, have I missed something? Why would one of them have to leave empty-handed? The prey 'learning a lesson' is not necessary for sating the hunger. That is mostly justification/a security measure not to attract Heroes. So... why should not both be able to feed off of the target?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think both can do a full feed off the same target, that's why I said or use family dinner. As for why one might walk away, it might just decide they want no part in what's coming up in the other's lesson.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1117196#post1117196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mention that, should they really have <i>opposite lessons </i>to teach, how come they are ending up with the <i>same </i>guy? Can't rightly say I see a Beast looking to teach the lesson of Pro-Slavery to a KKK member. What kind of person would be an approrpiate candidate for the lesson of finally stopping/starting relying on others?<br /> <br /> I mean, theoretically, there is nothing stopping them, and how it turns out completely depends on the beasts in question and their relationship imo. But still, I wonder what qualities you possess to attract two Beasts at the same time for opposite reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being undecided on an issue would lead to being percieved as able to go either way. I've known tons of people that if you say you don't really have an opinion on certain political things they'll immediatly jump on you saying how it is irresponsible not to have an opinion because this is really important and while you're at it you should totally be on their side of the issue. Then there's also misunderstanding a stance, I've seen cases where a person tries to keep their opinion on a subject quiet resulted in people presuming the person was clearly on x side of the argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T15:17:15-07:00","id":1117469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1117196#post1117196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, have I missed something? Why would one of them have to leave empty-handed? The prey 'learning a lesson' is not necessary for sating the hunger. That is mostly justification/a security measure not to attract Heroes. So... why should not both be able to feed off of the target?<br /> <br /> Not to mention that, should they really have <i>opposite lessons </i>to teach, how come they are ending up with the <i>same </i>guy? Can't rightly say I see a Beast looking to teach the lesson of Pro-Slavery to a KKK member. What kind of person would be an approrpiate candidate for the lesson of finally stopping/starting relying on others?<br /> <br /> I mean, theoretically, there is nothing stopping them, and how it turns out completely depends on the beasts in question and their relationship imo. But still, I wonder what qualities you possess to attract two Beasts at the same time for opposite reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume that the beasts are objective. If Beast A sees some guy, working at a fast food place, is impressed by his whatever and thinks something like &quot;He looks like the kind of person who is living way below his potential! I gotta scare some effort into him!&quot;, then it's not too far fetched that another beast might run into the same guy bragging about his ambitions and thinks &quot;He is obviously being too ambitious and is risking his safety! He should be happy with what he has.&quot;.<br /> Beast A comes back later, sees the guy still being in his old place and the dance might start. Well, at least until the guy kills himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T18:52:19-07:00","id":1117531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1117329#post1117329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being undecided on an issue would lead to being percieved as able to go either way. I've known tons of people that if you say you don't really have an opinion on certain political things they'll immediatly jump on you saying how it is irresponsible not to have an opinion because this is really important and while you're at it you should totally be on their side of the issue. Then there's also misunderstanding a stance, I've seen cases where a person tries to keep their opinion on a subject quiet resulted in people presuming the person was clearly on x side of the argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... is actually a very good point! I concur.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13654\" data-vbnamecard=\"13654\">Davesknd</a> huh. But this way, they would feed alternately on one guy, no? That isn't a good idea for a lot of reasons in the first place, but I guess I can see where you're coming from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T15:02:03-07:00","id":1124490,"title":"","content":"Btw, the book has something to say on this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 230</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conflict of Hungers: A Ravager burns down a building<br /> containing an object a Collector was hoping to steal.<br /> A Predator injures a corrupt politician before he can<br /> stumble into the Nemesis\u2019 trap. A Tyrant chases down<br /> her target, only to find that another Beast\u2019s lesson has<br /> rendered him too fragile to endure her predations.<br /> Conflict of Hunger tends to be an easy misunderstanding<br /> to fix; just the kind of thing that happens when<br /> Beasts hunt in the same areas. If it happens more than<br /> once, however, it starts to look less like coincidence and<br /> more like deliberate action, and then it\u2019s not uncommon<br /> for one Beast to short-circuit another\u2019s hunts just to<br /> get back at him. Feuds escalate, Beasts get their broods<br /> involved, and in short order they\u2019re enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:39:22-07:00","id":1124831,"title":"","content":"The teachings are just a pretextso Beasts can live with themselves, so yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T04:03:41-07:00","id":1125529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1124831#post1124831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The teachings are just a pretextso Beasts can live with themselves, so yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the &quot;so Beasts can live with themselves&quot; part is key. If the importance of lessons and the benefit to the target in learning them, are lies, then they're lies the Beasts are telling themselves first and foremost - and it would be hard to sustain that illusion without objecting to someone teaching your target a contrary lesson at the same time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1115228#post1115228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though it would be kind of interesting if a peace between two Beasts with an irreconcilable lesson conflict just decided to force the breaking point, feed, and then leave and let the person come to their own conclusions about what the frack they've learned during this whole mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could do that too, on the assumption that no one knows what the target needs better than their own primordial subconscious.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T23:12:33-07:00","id":1125804,"title":"","content":"When you get right down to it, the whole teaching lessons thing is just an excuse anyways. The Horror doesn't care if its victim learns something in the process, it just wants to slake its hunger.<br /> <br /> I imagine that a brood consisting of multiple different families or hungers would run into a situation like this rather frequently. Each of the families embody a different fear, and each hunger resonates with a different lesson. So having a bunch of different Beasts come to a consensus on how and what to teach would be a pipe dream. The best they could do is compromise and try not to step on each others' toes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T21:57:03-07:00","id":1126175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1125804#post1125804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you get right down to it, the whole teaching lessons thing is just an excuse anyways. The Horror doesn't care if its victim learns something in the process, it just wants to slake its hunger.<br /> <br /> I imagine that a brood consisting of multiple different families or hungers would run into a situation like this rather frequently. Each of the families embody a different fear, and each hunger resonates with a different lesson. So having a bunch of different Beasts come to a consensus on how and what to teach would be a pipe dream. The best they could do is compromise and try not to step on each others' toes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most ironic thing though? It's pretty likely that Beasts with their varying Lessons are HARMING the Primordial Dream even more.<br /> <br /> That because so many different types of Lessons are being taught at once, often with different and contradictory messages, that means mortals become very confused on what Lessons they are supposed to be learning versus what they aren't supposed to learn.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Fearful Lesson Dark Era even sort of hints at this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Fearful Lesson, p. 242</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Observing how Beasts interacted with the South may offer a clearer perspective on why Reconstruction failed. After all, a Beast\u2019s most emotionally (and ethically) fulfilling meal usually comes when her victim learns an important lesson. Without a sense of purpose or cultural unity, these lessons lose their meaning. A white supremacist might wake up to the pain she has caused, but a different man gets taught the perils of supporting black voting rights.<br /> <br /> <b>Eventually, any meaningful signal gets lost and everything becomes little more than noise. Prejudice reinforces prejudice, and no one can find their way forward.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T23:49:51-07:00","id":1126205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1126175#post1126175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The most ironic thing though? It's pretty likely that Beasts with their varying Lessons are HARMING the Primordial Dream even more.<br /> <br /> That because so many different types of Lessons are being taught at once, often with different and contradictory messages, that means mortals become very confused on what Lessons they are supposed to be learning versus what they aren't supposed to learn.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, they are not harming it. The primordial dream is the collective subconscious of the species' roots. It's the world as seen through the eyes of hunter-gatherers. Xenophobia, bigotry and the like are not bugs of the primordial dream, they are features (having heightened group cohesion when outsiders encroach, dividing the world in clear-cut categories, whipping yourself into a hateful frenzy before contact). The primordial dream at it's purest would be modern society collapsing and everyone sitting around the campfire again and telling each other of the giant monsters they saw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T23:59:37-07:00","id":1126206,"title":"","content":"The increased number of Beasts is probably causing problems for the Primordial Dream, but I don't imagine it's in any more of a complication than just what's happened due to the massive spike in human population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:57:59-07:00","id":1127118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114545-do-the-lessons-a-beast-teaches-have-to-agree-with-each-other?p=1126205#post1126205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, they are not harming it. The primordial dream is the collective subconscious of the species' roots. It's the world as seen through the eyes of hunter-gatherers. Xenophobia, bigotry and the like are not bugs of the primordial dream, they are features (having heightened group cohesion when outsiders encroach, dividing the world in clear-cut categories, whipping yourself into a hateful frenzy before contact). The primordial dream at it's purest would be modern society collapsing and everyone sitting around the campfire again and telling each other of the giant monsters they saw.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Exactly. It's called the <b>Primordial</b> Dream for a reason, it goes back to our most primal fears from the dawn of our species. No matter what form they take, Beasts still embody the basic fears of weakness, darkness, exposure, revulsion and being out of your element.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the great olden days, an Anakim may have stemmed from the fear of large beasts who required entire hunting parties to bring down safely. In the modern nights, they might be the CEO of a mega-corporation who buys up all the good property and runs small businesses out of town. The only way to stop their aggressive business expansion is for the whole town / city to come together and fight back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-10-2017, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}